This repository (the data, its structure, selection and arrangement, and the
documentation) is made public so that people can contribute to it. Except as
stated below, no license is granted.

1. What you may do

   You may view this repository on GitHub, and fork it on GitHub solely to
   prepare and submit pull requests to this repository.

2. What you may not do

   Without prior written permission from the maintainers, you may not, in whole
   or in part, for commercial or non-commercial purposes:

   a. copy, download in bulk, scrape, mirror or archive the data;
   b. publish, redistribute, sell, sublicense or otherwise make it available;
   c. use it in, or to build, any website, app, API, product, service or
      dataset;
   d. use it to train, fine-tune, evaluate or ground any machine learning or
      AI model or system.

3. Contributions

   By submitting a pull request, issue or other contribution, you confirm that
   you have the right to submit it, and you grant the maintainers a perpetual,
   worldwide, irrevocable, royalty-free, non-exclusive license to use, copy,
   modify, publish, sublicense and distribute your contribution, as part of
   this repository and in any product built from it. You keep any rights you
   have in your contribution.

4. Third-party data

   Sections 1 and 2 cover only what the maintainers own. Some records come
   from others and keep their own terms:

   a. Events with "dataset": "ai-layoffs-index" come from the AI Layoffs Index
      (https://ailayoffs.org), under its license
      (https://ailayoffs.org/license). Its terms apply to those records:
      attribute the AI Layoffs Index and each event's sources, and keep
      citations dated.
   b. Part of the historical data was compiled with reference to layoffs.fyi
      (https://layoffs.fyi), credited as it asks; see README.md.
   c. Every event links the press articles it is based on. Those articles,
      their titles, descriptions and images belong to their publishers. The
      link previews stored here only point to them.

5. Third-party names

   Company names, logos and trademarks belong to their owners. Their
   appearance here does not imply endorsement.

6. Removal requests

   If you represent a company or a publisher and want information removed or
   corrected, open an issue in this repository.

7. No warranty

   The data is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. Figures are
   taken from the linked press coverage and may be incomplete or out of date.
   The maintainers are not liable for any claim or damages arising from it.

To ask for permission to use the data, open an issue in this repository.
